\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Internal Clifford directions}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the \vocabk{internal exterior module}{fdip-00YE} and its form,
write #{v\wedge} for left multiplication by #{v}. Write
#{b(v,-)\cdot} for the contraction which kills #{1} and satisfies
##{\begin{aligned}
&(b(v,-)\cdot)(w_1\wedge\cdots\wedge w_p)\\
&\qquad=\sum_{j=1}^p(-1)^{j-1}b(v,w_j)
 w_1\wedge\cdots\wedge\widehat{w_j}\wedge\cdots\wedge w_p.
\end{aligned}}
The \vocab{internal Clifford direction} associated to #{v} is
#{c(v)=(v\wedge)+(b(v,-)\cdot)} on #{E}. This contraction
uses the internal form, not a cubical direction.}
